WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.940
The Hunt for Red October.

00:00:02.380 --> 00:00:03.940
Join the Hunt.

00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:27.180
And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:28.840
I'm Mike. I'm Sean.

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:30.120
And I'm Joe.

00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:39.760
The Hunt for Red October, a very serious film, maybe one of the most serious films we've covered in video game 8-bit form since Platoon.

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:48.640
Yeah, you know, like, I feel like some of these are weird when they get video games and The Hunt for Red October is no exception.

00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:57.740
It starts very serious even on the video game with a wall of text and I just know every kid in America hits start as soon as that stuff started coming up on screen.

00:00:57.740 --> 00:01:04.920
Especially because it's like, it's all like American history and I feel like, you know, if you're like eight years old, you're like, okay, I'm not reading that.

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:07.160
It very much is not American history.

00:01:07.420 --> 00:01:08.440
It's just the plot of the movie.

00:01:08.440 --> 00:01:15.460
Yeah, but I mean, November 12th, 1984, approximately four months before, you know, the Soviet Union and...

00:01:15.460 --> 00:01:16.900
Come on. No, it's like serious.

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:19.300
It's serious. It means video games are serious.

00:01:19.460 --> 00:01:21.440
It means that you're important for playing it.

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:25.220
Come on. Look, I'm not saying I don't like it now.

00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:29.400
I'm just saying that I feel like a lot of kids, they're skipping through that.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:33.000
I think you're thinking of the current generation.

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:35.920
I'm thinking of me when I was eight.

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:43.020
Oh, okay. Yeah, 1984 to me would have sounded forever ago, even in 1991.

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:50.460
Probably. Now, Sean, you are repeating some government lies there about this just being part of the movie.

00:01:50.800 --> 00:02:01.240
I want to remind you that it's repeated statements by both the Soviet and American governments is that nothing that we are about to see in this video game ever happened, all caps.

00:02:01.240 --> 00:02:05.060
So are you just perpetuating that myth here on the podcast as well?

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:09.300
Because I'm inclined to believe that at least some of this happened.

00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:14.520
Well, if we pull up Jack Ryan on the phone, maybe he could give us a bit more info.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:17.240
Yeah, so is this our first Tom Clancy game?

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:19.840
Like, is this like the beginning of the Tom Clancy games?

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:23.060
And it makes sense because this is also his first novel.

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:24.820
See, because the...

00:02:24.820 --> 00:02:26.360
We're getting Ghost Recon soon.

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:29.680
The back of the box makes me feel like it's going to be...

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:33.840
Join the hunt makes me feel like it's going to be like a Pokemon Go, like, ARG style.

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:37.820
Like, everyone is out there hunting for the Red October on their phone.

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:40.320
In submarines, do you have to be in water for this?

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:45.320
Yes. It's like the Pokemon Go won't be in the water instead of land.

00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:46.960
But you can still give it a shot.

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:54.840
True. Now, Tom Clancy, notable for the video game section, sure, but probably more prolific as a writer.

00:02:55.620 --> 00:02:58.520
I'm interested in both sides because I never really played...

00:02:58.520 --> 00:03:03.320
There are tons of Tom Clancy's Splinter Cell, Tom Clancy's Ghost Recon.

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:06.260
There's plenty of those games. I never really played most of any of that.

00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:10.600
So I'd be interested both from like a video game and literature perspective.

00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:13.800
What's your exposure to the Tom Clancy-verse?

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:19.740
Almost nothing other than like knowing what these video games are and knowing they're based on books.

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:21.840
Like, that's it.

00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:25.080
Okay, so Sean's going to have to carry this segment.

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:26.140
Please, this episode.

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:29.460
Well, just this segment, just about Tom Clancy.

00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:30.560
You played the game, right?

00:03:30.760 --> 00:03:32.760
No. You didn't play this game?

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:35.640
I haven't played one of these games in months.

00:03:35.740 --> 00:03:36.580
You guys just haven't noticed.

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:41.320
You're doing a great job or we're doing a really bad job.

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:47.080
Yeah. Well, yeah, I've played some Tom Clancy stuff.

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:49.960
I've seen some Tom Clancy movies.

00:03:50.180 --> 00:03:56.320
I haven't read a Tom Clancy book, but I'd never say never.

00:03:57.580 --> 00:03:59.520
But yeah, Splinter Cell was great.

00:03:59.820 --> 00:04:03.740
I played some Rainbow Six Siege for a little bit when that was new.

00:04:04.940 --> 00:04:11.140
I played some Rainbow Six when it wasn't a games-of-service thing.

00:04:11.900 --> 00:04:14.680
Yeah, I've done some Tom Clancy's.

00:04:15.140 --> 00:04:17.840
But it's not always, is the focus on stealth?

00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:21.740
No, the focus is on military.

00:04:22.280 --> 00:04:27.420
Right, so Splinter Cell is like the stealth adjacent but still military category?

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:36.280
I actually don't know if it's based on anything or if he just sort of workshopped the idea with them and then allowed them.

00:04:36.520 --> 00:04:39.740
Or if he just let them put his name on it.

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:42.120
Right, which could very well happen.

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:45.820
Yeah, but no, he's not a stealth writer.

00:04:45.820 --> 00:04:46.980
He's a military writer.

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:53.980
Right. Yeah, I guess I always assumed that Splinter Cell was the answer to Metal Gear.

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:55.660
I guess in a way, yeah.

00:04:55.660 --> 00:04:59.280
And in terms of the books, not really.

00:04:59.460 --> 00:05:04.040
But I mean, Tom Clancy's had many things adapted into movies as well.

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:10.640
He's kind of like the spy military thriller version of Stephen King.

00:05:11.260 --> 00:05:21.840
Yeah, or the non-horror Dean Koontz is actually, I think, a better thing there for me.

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:25.840
I think it talks more about the quality.

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:34.260
The quality. And then how about the actual movie, The Hunt for Red October, with Sean Connery and Alec Baldwin?

00:05:34.260 --> 00:05:35.940
Any watchers of that?

00:05:36.360 --> 00:05:37.540
I read the back flap.

00:05:37.880 --> 00:05:39.300
I watched the trailer.

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:43.540
I watched the movie clips, selection of nine scenes.

00:05:44.120 --> 00:05:48.460
I probably saw the movie when I was much younger, but I don't remember much of it now.

00:05:48.460 --> 00:05:55.380
I feel like I have a vague memory of maybe having watched it with my dad or something, but I don't remember it at all, if I did.

00:05:55.520 --> 00:05:57.700
The Hunt for Red October. Yes.

00:05:57.700 --> 00:06:04.820
I know that you got the classic Sean Connery voice in there, but that's all I know about it.

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:09.760
And he's doing a good job of what the character is.

00:06:09.980 --> 00:06:13.640
The character, it's unknown his motives, right?

00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:16.400
Is he going to attack the U.S.

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:17.960
or is he defecting to the U.S.?

00:06:19.020 --> 00:06:26.400
And I think Sean Connery plays the character in a way where you could rag on him for just being Sean Connery,

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:34.460
but you could also say that he's doing this really good, riding the cusp of absurdity on his character as well.

00:06:34.540 --> 00:06:36.580
And I enjoyed his performance in this film.

00:06:36.700 --> 00:06:42.400
I also enjoyed Alec Baldwin in this film, and it kind of made me wonder what happened to Alec Baldwin a little bit.

00:06:42.460 --> 00:06:48.120
Because at this time in his life, he's doing so many big, big movies.

00:06:48.720 --> 00:06:53.320
Blockbusters is questionable on some of these things, but just prolific films.

00:06:53.320 --> 00:06:56.840
And I feel like we just, ever since he shot that person, we don't hear from him anymore.

00:06:57.680 --> 00:06:58.760
Well, I guess that makes sense.

00:06:59.700 --> 00:07:01.380
Yeah, well, you got to go there, huh?

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:04.860
Yeah, well, it happened to him, but I'd say even before that he dropped off.

00:07:04.920 --> 00:07:08.240
Maybe he dropped off when Cat in the Hat came out, but I would argue that was his peak.

00:07:08.660 --> 00:07:17.400
I mean, I know him most as, like, a comedic actor with 30 Rock, but I'm probably in the minority there.

00:07:17.820 --> 00:07:21.960
Well, I feel like that became such a part of his brand, is that, like,

00:07:21.960 --> 00:07:26.200
so serious it's not serious kind of humor.

00:07:26.660 --> 00:07:29.860
Yeah. That's a great description of that.

00:07:31.400 --> 00:07:35.060
And I guess, you know, submarines are pretty cool themselves, right?

00:07:35.080 --> 00:07:40.240
I think we covered that in our silent service episode, that submarine simulators,

00:07:40.460 --> 00:07:45.120
or just the idea of controlling a submarine as a unique vehicle, is pretty cool.

00:07:45.120 --> 00:07:51.820
And the Hunt for Red October submarine has an experimental caterpillar drive feature,

00:07:52.120 --> 00:08:00.080
which, pretty central to the plot, makes it so that it can basically become invisible underwater and not be detected.

00:08:00.500 --> 00:08:03.780
And that's something that's obviously going to fit into the game, too.

00:08:04.620 --> 00:08:09.220
But since you were talking about, Joe, watching it with your dad, maybe, perhaps.

00:08:09.580 --> 00:08:13.680
It's like, I do think that that's also, like, kind of how this audience fits in, too, though,

00:08:13.780 --> 00:08:20.140
is that, like, if you were a kid, the movie was probably, like, cool, like, to look at,

00:08:20.180 --> 00:08:23.020
but you didn't understand really, like, what was going on,

00:08:23.040 --> 00:08:25.820
or you were, like, maybe a little bored by, like, the dialogue stuff,

00:08:25.820 --> 00:08:28.240
and you were like, ah, can't they just get back to the submarine footage?

00:08:29.280 --> 00:08:32.300
So the game, rightfully, gives you, it's all submarine.

00:08:32.620 --> 00:08:34.080
It's, like, the idea is just...

00:08:34.080 --> 00:08:34.920
Well, not the cutscenes.

00:08:35.080 --> 00:08:38.260
It's got those cutscenes that you feel like they're lifted right out of the movie.

00:08:38.300 --> 00:08:39.960
I think they might be ported from the movie.

00:08:41.720 --> 00:08:43.140
Like FMVs, but for NES.

00:08:43.520 --> 00:08:48.000
Yeah, yeah. But the submarine is basically the maker break of the game,

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:51.080
and the gameplay, it's very interesting.

00:08:51.380 --> 00:08:53.920
Obviously, on the NES, they're not going to try to, like,

00:08:54.480 --> 00:08:55.620
faithfully recreate the movie.

00:08:55.680 --> 00:08:58.040
How could they? I'm not even sure what that would look like.

00:08:58.240 --> 00:09:02.620
But instead of recreating a submarine simulator, even,

00:09:02.880 --> 00:09:05.780
the NES version turns into kind of a...

00:09:05.780 --> 00:09:06.840
Oops, all shmup.

00:09:07.200 --> 00:09:08.700
Well, is it a shmup, though?

00:09:08.880 --> 00:09:09.900
It's a shmup.

00:09:10.180 --> 00:09:11.000
I don't know.

00:09:11.360 --> 00:09:14.460
I don't know either, because, like, on paper, really,

00:09:14.600 --> 00:09:17.080
the only thing that differentiates it from a shmup

00:09:17.080 --> 00:09:19.560
is that, like, you kind of control the camera.

00:09:20.320 --> 00:09:21.900
Even that's not fully true.

00:09:22.140 --> 00:09:26.520
Yeah. But that, like, small difference, you sort of do.

00:09:26.520 --> 00:09:28.540
It just moves really slow if you're not moving it,

00:09:28.560 --> 00:09:30.320
but you decide to speed it up.

00:09:30.420 --> 00:09:34.280
Like, you're moving it forward faster than it's, like,

00:09:34.820 --> 00:09:37.400
than it's regular, like, automatic movement.

00:09:37.660 --> 00:09:41.420
But, like, that little tiny difference does make it feel very different

00:09:41.420 --> 00:09:42.300
than a shmup to me.

00:09:42.600 --> 00:09:45.760
It makes the movement feel different to me.

00:09:45.760 --> 00:09:49.100
I feel like it's ignoring a lot of the rules of shmups, too.

00:09:49.220 --> 00:09:50.240
Like, it's very...

00:09:51.180 --> 00:09:53.940
Even with the other enemies, like, it's not some...

00:09:53.940 --> 00:09:55.460
Not that it has to be a bullet hell or whatever,

00:09:55.560 --> 00:09:58.260
but there's not really, like, a screen littered with enemies

00:09:58.260 --> 00:09:59.180
where you're constantly clearing stuff.

00:09:59.240 --> 00:10:01.380
It is more like action navigation,

00:10:01.980 --> 00:10:03.580
getting through these obstacles

00:10:03.580 --> 00:10:10.180
and the ability to fire both head-on and above you.

00:10:10.180 --> 00:10:13.200
So there's definitely some things going on here

00:10:13.200 --> 00:10:14.580
that could bring it up to discussion.

00:10:14.580 --> 00:10:17.200
But I wouldn't say calling it a shmup is unfair, Sean,

00:10:17.300 --> 00:10:18.560
because at the end of the day,

00:10:18.680 --> 00:10:21.740
all you're doing is controlling this vehicle

00:10:21.740 --> 00:10:25.360
like you would any other vehicle in these horizontal games

00:10:26.440 --> 00:10:29.820
across from a beginning to end to get to a destination.

00:10:30.740 --> 00:10:34.620
And even, like, the places you play in the game,

00:10:34.700 --> 00:10:37.780
it's just kind of like, where is this on Earth?

00:10:38.200 --> 00:10:39.080
It's in the ocean.

00:10:39.700 --> 00:10:41.900
Yeah, but where do they have, like, giant walls

00:10:41.900 --> 00:10:45.740
and retractable pipes and, like, where does that all exist?

00:10:45.740 --> 00:10:46.620
I assume those were, like...

00:10:46.620 --> 00:10:50.560
In the ocean. Yeah, that's just, like, on the beach

00:10:50.560 --> 00:10:51.680
that you already see that stuff.

00:10:51.840 --> 00:10:53.060
You're not going to be, like, waist deep

00:10:53.060 --> 00:10:54.700
and you're already seeing that stuff.

00:10:54.900 --> 00:10:58.420
And I don't know or pretend to know anything about submarines.

00:10:58.580 --> 00:10:59.520
Most of my submarine knowledge

00:10:59.520 --> 00:11:02.260
comes from the aforementioned silent service.

00:11:02.580 --> 00:11:05.720
But is it really that easy to move a submarine in reverse?

00:11:05.720 --> 00:11:09.180
Is it really that easy to just, like, back up a submarine

00:11:09.180 --> 00:11:10.160
like it is in this game?

00:11:10.480 --> 00:11:13.900
It's almost as if, like, they're calling it...

00:11:13.900 --> 00:11:16.720
It's almost as if, like, the control scheme, for the most part,

00:11:16.860 --> 00:11:18.600
is sort of ported from shmups.

00:11:19.300 --> 00:11:21.180
See, all right, here's the thing, though.

00:11:21.420 --> 00:11:25.300
I guess, for me, just being able to come to a complete stop

00:11:25.820 --> 00:11:27.960
feels not super shmup-like to me.

00:11:28.460 --> 00:11:29.400
That's a very...

00:11:29.400 --> 00:11:31.980
I think you guys have a very narrow description

00:11:31.980 --> 00:11:33.620
of what shmups are.

00:11:33.620 --> 00:11:36.140
Well, all right, that's one of the elements.

00:11:36.280 --> 00:11:38.200
But also, like, a shmup, like Mike was saying, too,

00:11:38.240 --> 00:11:41.200
I feel like a shmup has, like, tons of targets on screen

00:11:41.200 --> 00:11:43.300
where I'm, like, shooting them up.

00:11:43.300 --> 00:11:45.120
It feels like I need to be shooting a lot

00:11:45.120 --> 00:11:46.080
at a lot of enemies.

00:11:46.080 --> 00:11:48.200
And there are portions of this game that are like that.

00:11:48.360 --> 00:11:49.920
But there are large portions of this game

00:11:49.920 --> 00:11:52.360
where it's, like, you're quietly navigating

00:11:52.360 --> 00:11:54.320
through, like, little rocks and everything.

00:11:54.760 --> 00:11:57.160
Yeah, you don't usually have a health bar in shmups, either.

00:11:57.520 --> 00:11:59.740
And I'm not saying that this definitely isn't a shmup.

00:11:59.840 --> 00:12:01.820
I'm just saying this does not feel like other shmups to me.

00:12:03.860 --> 00:12:09.480
It's a very polished and with a few extra bells and whistles shmup.

00:12:09.840 --> 00:12:14.960
But we could have this conversation the whole episode if we want.

00:12:15.440 --> 00:12:17.300
Yeah, I think we should. I think we should continue to.

00:12:18.200 --> 00:12:22.200
In the favor of shmups, as I mentioned, with your primary weapons,

00:12:22.440 --> 00:12:24.960
the A button firing torpedoes horizontally

00:12:24.960 --> 00:12:27.680
and the B button firing missiles vertically

00:12:27.680 --> 00:12:31.780
because you have enemies both above and to the side of you.

00:12:31.900 --> 00:12:33.140
So you have to deal with them.

00:12:33.820 --> 00:12:37.760
There are making a lot of good use of the NES controller, though,

00:12:37.860 --> 00:12:40.080
because the select button is also what you use

00:12:40.080 --> 00:12:43.320
to activate the Caterpillar drive we were talking about,

00:12:43.520 --> 00:12:46.060
which helps the Red October, which is—

00:12:46.060 --> 00:12:47.040
I feel like we didn't mention this.

00:12:47.160 --> 00:12:49.040
The Red October is the name of the submarine.

00:12:49.040 --> 00:12:51.440
It's not what they're hunting for.

00:12:51.960 --> 00:12:54.160
Everybody else is hunting the Red October.

00:12:55.100 --> 00:12:59.520
And so you press the select button to kind of evade enemies.

00:12:59.820 --> 00:13:02.700
And then if you press A and B together,

00:13:03.560 --> 00:13:06.760
you get basically your emergency defense system,

00:13:07.120 --> 00:13:12.560
your decoys, electronic countermeasures,

00:13:12.600 --> 00:13:13.620
I think they're called in the manual,

00:13:13.840 --> 00:13:17.020
that attract and destroy nearby income enemy fire, too.

00:13:17.160 --> 00:13:19.760
So those are all neat features that I think

00:13:19.760 --> 00:13:21.620
would actually welcome in a shmup, right?

00:13:21.620 --> 00:13:24.800
A select button that kind of turns your vehicle temporarily invisible,

00:13:25.800 --> 00:13:27.520
pressing the two buttons together

00:13:27.520 --> 00:13:32.500
to temporarily send a decoy out that could take hits for you.

00:13:32.620 --> 00:13:34.020
Those all sound like great ideas.

00:13:34.280 --> 00:13:35.480
Do they work in the game?

00:13:39.900 --> 00:13:41.040
It's hard to say,

00:13:41.080 --> 00:13:43.760
because I feel like some of them work in like—

00:13:44.210 --> 00:13:47.080
you know, you need decent power-ups.

00:13:47.180 --> 00:13:48.690
I'm trying to be careful of not further—

00:13:49.110 --> 00:13:50.070
making it sound like a shmup.

00:13:50.270 --> 00:13:51.710
—too much by making it be like,

00:13:51.790 --> 00:13:53.930
wow, these are really shmup elements I'm talking about here.

00:13:58.470 --> 00:14:00.310
But, like, yeah, there's—

00:14:00.870 --> 00:14:03.150
I didn't find myself using them very often.

00:14:03.230 --> 00:14:05.630
Granted, I didn't get super far in this game.

00:14:05.630 --> 00:14:09.670
It's very, very difficult for me just to navigate through these waters.

00:14:09.850 --> 00:14:11.490
So, like, you know, maybe later in the game,

00:14:11.510 --> 00:14:13.030
I would have used them a lot more.

00:14:13.030 --> 00:14:15.490
But for me, I think I just didn't—

00:14:15.490 --> 00:14:17.130
I didn't end up using them.

00:14:17.210 --> 00:14:19.170
Like, I used them to, like, test them out and see what they are,

00:14:19.250 --> 00:14:20.530
and then I kind of forgot about them a lot.

00:14:20.810 --> 00:14:23.130
Yeah, I think they mostly work.

00:14:23.290 --> 00:14:26.270
I did forget about countermeasures pretty often,

00:14:26.270 --> 00:14:28.330
but the—

00:14:29.090 --> 00:14:30.250
basically, it's like a—

00:14:30.250 --> 00:14:31.130
it's a force field.

00:14:31.310 --> 00:14:33.350
It's not really anything about, like,

00:14:33.950 --> 00:14:35.290
running silent or anything.

00:14:35.490 --> 00:14:36.990
But that I would use,

00:14:36.990 --> 00:14:38.170
because there's a lot of situations

00:14:38.170 --> 00:14:40.830
where you just sort of get pelted,

00:14:41.990 --> 00:14:44.190
and your armor will melt

00:14:44.910 --> 00:14:47.330
if too much stuff happens to you at once.

00:14:50.050 --> 00:14:51.910
I did like the—

00:14:53.050 --> 00:14:56.170
I did like the way that you move in this game,

00:14:56.190 --> 00:14:58.990
where, like, you kind of do have to get real—

00:15:00.590 --> 00:15:02.150
real precise with it,

00:15:02.170 --> 00:15:02.990
because you're—

00:15:03.970 --> 00:15:05.770
depending on if you go up or down,

00:15:05.770 --> 00:15:07.050
you kind of—

00:15:07.050 --> 00:15:08.130
I don't know. What is that?

00:15:08.170 --> 00:15:09.210
That's not— is it roll?

00:15:09.270 --> 00:15:11.010
That's not roll. Is it yaw?

00:15:11.430 --> 00:15:14.030
Is it— you kind of tilt up.

00:15:14.270 --> 00:15:16.610
You tilt forward and backward,

00:15:16.770 --> 00:15:18.670
and that changes your hitbox,

00:15:18.850 --> 00:15:24.950
and you can do that to avoid torpedoes.

00:15:24.970 --> 00:15:28.010
You can do that to sort of thread the needle

00:15:28.010 --> 00:15:32.550
through very narrow sections of the game,

00:15:32.550 --> 00:15:35.550
because you do go into a lot of caves

00:15:35.550 --> 00:15:40.710
for a massive Soviet submarine,

00:15:41.390 --> 00:15:43.570
more than I would think for something like that.

00:15:44.650 --> 00:15:45.830
Armed caves, too.

00:15:46.070 --> 00:15:47.650
There's a lot of, like,

00:15:47.830 --> 00:15:50.230
attached turrets and everything in those caves.

00:15:50.950 --> 00:15:52.350
And I guess also, like,

00:15:53.210 --> 00:15:54.430
flamethrowers at certain points.

00:15:54.450 --> 00:15:55.710
I don't know what those are supposed to be.

00:15:55.710 --> 00:16:00.170
But, yeah, I liked how the game felt, for sure.

00:16:00.430 --> 00:16:02.230
Yeah, I think that that's, like—

00:16:02.230 --> 00:16:04.910
that was the shining star of this game

00:16:04.910 --> 00:16:07.270
was the feel of the motion.

00:16:07.410 --> 00:16:08.670
The tilt part you're talking about,

00:16:08.670 --> 00:16:11.450
I also used a lot for just shooting

00:16:11.450 --> 00:16:13.290
at a slight tilt upwards.

00:16:13.290 --> 00:16:15.170
And, you know,

00:16:15.250 --> 00:16:17.270
if you're just talking about it,

00:16:17.450 --> 00:16:19.330
the gameplay, you might be like,

00:16:19.350 --> 00:16:21.970
well, that's annoying. Like, why can't I shoot at an angle

00:16:21.970 --> 00:16:24.370
without tilting the whole ship up or whatever?

00:16:24.790 --> 00:16:26.050
But, like, we gotta remember,

00:16:26.190 --> 00:16:28.230
we're talking about a submarine, and, like, I did appreciate

00:16:28.230 --> 00:16:29.350
that that was, like, a way

00:16:29.350 --> 00:16:30.850
that they translated, like,

00:16:31.310 --> 00:16:33.130
the way a submarine might work,

00:16:33.250 --> 00:16:34.350
where, like, there's not, like,

00:16:34.570 --> 00:16:36.650
a turret that you're able to tilt up

00:16:36.650 --> 00:16:37.490
and down independently

00:16:37.490 --> 00:16:40.170
of the sub itself.

00:16:40.770 --> 00:16:41.810
But then also, like,

00:16:42.330 --> 00:16:44.850
something about the floatiness of, like—

00:16:44.850 --> 00:16:46.810
or, like, the flow of the way you move.

00:16:46.990 --> 00:16:48.270
It's, like, a little bit slower,

00:16:48.330 --> 00:16:49.310
but it's really fluid,

00:16:49.310 --> 00:16:50.850
and it makes it feel, like,

00:16:51.390 --> 00:16:52.790
underwater and not in space.

00:16:52.790 --> 00:16:55.330
And I think that that, you know,

00:16:55.430 --> 00:16:56.970
that, like, helped sell it

00:16:56.970 --> 00:16:57.850
a little bit for me.

00:16:58.070 --> 00:17:00.570
Yeah, and the movement on the sub

00:17:00.570 --> 00:17:01.550
is very important

00:17:01.550 --> 00:17:03.710
to those claustrophobic sections

00:17:03.710 --> 00:17:05.770
because, specifically,

00:17:05.930 --> 00:17:08.190
once you get out of the Soviet harbor,

00:17:08.450 --> 00:17:11.490
which is that one with the ridiculous giant gates

00:17:11.490 --> 00:17:14.390
and pressure systems and stuff

00:17:14.390 --> 00:17:15.730
that you have to, like, time to get through,

00:17:15.730 --> 00:17:16.670
once you're, like,

00:17:16.870 --> 00:17:18.130
actually just, like, in the Arctic

00:17:18.130 --> 00:17:20.070
or the coral reefs

00:17:20.070 --> 00:17:22.070
or whatever. Or the crystal caverns

00:17:22.070 --> 00:17:23.550
in the Atlantic. Yeah, yeah, of course,

00:17:23.670 --> 00:17:24.730
the famous crystal caverns.

00:17:25.030 --> 00:17:26.290
Like, those sections,

00:17:27.510 --> 00:17:28.910
you know, may not be—

00:17:29.330 --> 00:17:30.570
may not have a lot of enemies,

00:17:30.590 --> 00:17:32.250
but you will just take a lot of damage

00:17:32.250 --> 00:17:33.790
if you don't know how to steer

00:17:33.790 --> 00:17:34.670
this thing properly.

00:17:34.670 --> 00:17:36.370
So a lot of it is also just, like,

00:17:36.630 --> 00:17:37.830
an impressive feat

00:17:37.830 --> 00:17:39.730
of knowing how to maneuver

00:17:39.730 --> 00:17:40.870
the Red October.

00:17:41.930 --> 00:17:42.890
Along the way, though,

00:17:43.010 --> 00:17:45.010
there are, like, you know, with your weapons,

00:17:45.010 --> 00:17:46.530
like, you can pick up upgrades

00:17:46.530 --> 00:17:48.870
for them, and both your horizontal

00:17:48.870 --> 00:17:50.010
and vertical weapon

00:17:50.010 --> 00:17:50.950
can be upgraded

00:17:50.950 --> 00:17:51.790
from short-range

00:17:51.790 --> 00:17:54.390
to long-range to even homing capabilities,

00:17:55.070 --> 00:17:57.250
but they also downgrade

00:17:57.250 --> 00:17:59.250
as your ammunition level falls.

00:17:59.470 --> 00:18:01.390
The only thing that can never disappear

00:18:01.390 --> 00:18:02.910
is torpedoes.

00:18:02.970 --> 00:18:04.570
You do have unlimited torpedoes.

00:18:04.650 --> 00:18:06.070
They just become weaker

00:18:06.070 --> 00:18:08.030
and slower, so you have to fire more of them.

00:18:08.710 --> 00:18:10.230
I think the game is, though,

00:18:10.330 --> 00:18:12.390
trying to balance, like,

00:18:12.390 --> 00:18:14.270
not even just the difference

00:18:14.270 --> 00:18:15.590
between navigation

00:18:15.590 --> 00:18:17.150
and enemy encounters,

00:18:17.150 --> 00:18:20.110
but also the different stages

00:18:20.110 --> 00:18:23.710
and, like, the feel of the game.

00:18:23.830 --> 00:18:25.290
Like, when you're in those coral reefs,

00:18:25.550 --> 00:18:27.330
you have a lot of enemies

00:18:27.330 --> 00:18:29.250
that are not necessarily

00:18:29.250 --> 00:18:31.870
in the water. They're above you parachuting in,

00:18:31.870 --> 00:18:33.630
or they're on boats,

00:18:33.670 --> 00:18:34.530
or they're on planes,

00:18:34.590 --> 00:18:36.510
and you don't have a lot of space

00:18:36.510 --> 00:18:38.330
because the reefs are, you know,

00:18:38.410 --> 00:18:39.490
like, you're very close to the water,

00:18:39.490 --> 00:18:40.690
so it's claustrophobic

00:18:40.690 --> 00:18:42.090
in a completely different way

00:18:42.090 --> 00:18:45.690
than the narrow cave segments

00:18:45.690 --> 00:18:46.950
because now you have, like,

00:18:47.410 --> 00:18:48.790
technically you're free to get around,

00:18:48.870 --> 00:18:50.350
but you have to kind of move through it quickly

00:18:50.350 --> 00:18:52.170
and dodge all this enemy fire.

00:18:52.510 --> 00:18:54.110
That particular stage...

00:18:54.110 --> 00:18:55.330
Yeah, that level was a pain in the ass.

00:18:55.670 --> 00:18:57.010
Yeah, so as I was going to say, particular stage,

00:18:57.130 --> 00:18:58.590
while it's early on, you know,

00:18:58.750 --> 00:19:00.370
you take a lot of damage early,

00:19:00.370 --> 00:19:02.870
and you have both, like,

00:19:02.930 --> 00:19:05.630
an armor to you,

00:19:05.730 --> 00:19:06.990
like an HP system that way,

00:19:07.030 --> 00:19:09.410
and a fuel system as well,

00:19:09.410 --> 00:19:11.330
and the fuel system is way more forgiving

00:19:11.330 --> 00:19:12.310
than the armor system,

00:19:12.510 --> 00:19:14.110
but if either one goes,

00:19:14.770 --> 00:19:15.970
it's game over.

00:19:16.470 --> 00:19:17.890
Well, you can run out of power.

00:19:18.730 --> 00:19:20.150
You just lose all of your...

00:19:20.150 --> 00:19:22.950
Oh, I didn't know that. You just lose, like, sonar.

00:19:25.370 --> 00:19:28.870
I think all of your abilities are weakened,

00:19:29.950 --> 00:19:31.810
but if you run out of power,

00:19:31.950 --> 00:19:32.810
you just get this thing

00:19:32.810 --> 00:19:34.370
that says out of power,

00:19:34.410 --> 00:19:36.270
but you can surface,

00:19:37.210 --> 00:19:41.090
and if you can dodge the, you know,

00:19:41.570 --> 00:19:43.830
bombing runs of these jets or whatever

00:19:46.110 --> 00:19:48.630
and not get hit by torpedoes from below,

00:19:49.010 --> 00:19:50.830
you just sort of hang there

00:19:50.830 --> 00:19:52.090
and recharge for a bit.

00:19:52.310 --> 00:19:53.710
Yeah, I kind of wish I knew that

00:19:53.710 --> 00:19:55.210
because I would have been more...

00:19:55.210 --> 00:19:57.390
I would have used my power more often.

00:19:57.950 --> 00:19:59.290
Yeah. Yeah, it's fun.

00:19:59.750 --> 00:20:01.830
It also just sort of drains on its own

00:20:01.830 --> 00:20:04.490
while you're below sea level.

00:20:04.490 --> 00:20:06.210
Yeah, but there's pickups for that, right?

00:20:06.310 --> 00:20:07.290
Yes. Yeah.

00:20:07.790 --> 00:20:09.330
Joe, you mentioned those cut scenes,

00:20:09.330 --> 00:20:12.390
and while they're definitely not FMVs,

00:20:12.470 --> 00:20:15.050
they are pretty long, dialogue-heavy,

00:20:15.630 --> 00:20:16.810
story-driven things.

00:20:16.930 --> 00:20:18.870
It's like, you could argue

00:20:18.870 --> 00:20:20.810
that it's necessary for a game

00:20:20.810 --> 00:20:23.110
based on a movie that is mostly just,

00:20:23.930 --> 00:20:27.050
you know, character-driven,

00:20:28.450 --> 00:20:30.250
you know, on the edge of your seat,

00:20:30.370 --> 00:20:33.290
what are they going to do next, decision-making style stuff,

00:20:33.310 --> 00:20:36.610
but it doesn't really translate to this game

00:20:36.610 --> 00:20:37.650
because then you just go back

00:20:37.650 --> 00:20:39.670
to, like, silly submarine-fighting.

00:20:40.990 --> 00:20:42.330
Yeah, I mean, yeah,

00:20:42.350 --> 00:20:44.130
it seems like it wasn't the most, like,

00:20:44.350 --> 00:20:45.890
smoothly implemented way

00:20:45.890 --> 00:20:49.070
to integrate the movie into the game,

00:20:49.090 --> 00:20:50.990
but you got to appreciate

00:20:50.990 --> 00:20:54.030
the very detailed talking heads

00:20:54.030 --> 00:20:56.970
of these characters, like, from the movie.

00:20:57.070 --> 00:20:59.930
I mean, like, particularly...

00:21:01.750 --> 00:21:03.770
I can't remember if it was the FBI agent

00:21:03.770 --> 00:21:05.130
or if it was Sean Connery.

00:21:05.130 --> 00:21:06.630
I think Sean Connery has, like,

00:21:06.810 --> 00:21:09.330
very distinct lighting on his face

00:21:09.330 --> 00:21:10.190
and he's, like...

00:21:10.190 --> 00:21:11.930
Well, he particularly is definitely, like...

00:21:11.930 --> 00:21:12.810
He, like, starts sweating

00:21:12.810 --> 00:21:13.810
when he says certain things

00:21:13.810 --> 00:21:15.550
and dabs the sweat off his forehead

00:21:15.550 --> 00:21:17.130
and, like, I feel the emotion in it.

00:21:17.170 --> 00:21:18.170
Is Sean Connery in these?

00:21:18.730 --> 00:21:20.250
Is that not Sean Connery?

00:21:20.370 --> 00:21:22.590
Well, the... The idea of Sean Connery.

00:21:22.790 --> 00:21:26.150
I'm pretty sure that this is, like, a...

00:21:26.150 --> 00:21:29.030
All this stuff is happening, like,

00:21:29.170 --> 00:21:30.850
not anywhere near the sub.

00:21:30.850 --> 00:21:35.470
Like, this is the, like, Soviet ambassador...

00:21:35.470 --> 00:21:36.510
Well, so remember, I don't...

00:21:36.510 --> 00:21:37.470
I haven't seen the movie.

00:21:37.630 --> 00:21:38.710
I don't know which character Sean Connery.

00:21:38.710 --> 00:21:39.710
Well, I just mean that none of them

00:21:39.710 --> 00:21:40.850
look like Sean Connery.

00:21:41.050 --> 00:21:42.270
I know, but aren't you...

00:21:42.270 --> 00:21:43.630
The guy in the tie, to me,

00:21:43.730 --> 00:21:44.830
looked like Sean Connery.

00:21:45.130 --> 00:21:47.130
No. The guy wiping the sweat off his forehead,

00:21:47.270 --> 00:21:48.610
I thought that that was Sean Connery.

00:21:48.810 --> 00:21:51.330
No, that's just, like, some Soviet ambassador dude.

00:21:52.770 --> 00:21:55.150
Right, but you are definitely playing

00:21:55.150 --> 00:21:57.910
as, you know, James Bond, if you will,

00:21:57.910 --> 00:22:00.770
in this game, because maybe the biggest reason

00:22:00.770 --> 00:22:02.330
why this isn't a shmup is because

00:22:02.330 --> 00:22:04.350
at the final stage, you finally take control

00:22:04.350 --> 00:22:08.310
of just Sean Connery, which we should...

00:22:08.310 --> 00:22:10.450
Marco Ramius, I believe, is his name.

00:22:11.330 --> 00:22:13.610
And you do a platforming stage,

00:22:13.810 --> 00:22:15.890
where it's, like, you know, you have a gun

00:22:15.890 --> 00:22:18.410
and you're fighting off other enemies on land,

00:22:18.410 --> 00:22:19.590
and you have to...

00:22:20.370 --> 00:22:22.810
You have to disarm the bombs

00:22:23.570 --> 00:22:25.210
that I think they're hooked up

00:22:25.210 --> 00:22:26.350
to the Red October itself.

00:22:26.930 --> 00:22:29.330
Yes, this is in the submarine.

00:22:29.510 --> 00:22:30.610
Right, so now you're in the submarine,

00:22:30.610 --> 00:22:32.170
so I guess that's what I was saying,

00:22:32.310 --> 00:22:34.690
is, like, you are playing as Sean Connery.

00:22:34.810 --> 00:22:36.150
Now you are, yeah.

00:22:36.510 --> 00:22:38.150
I felt this was very confusing.

00:22:38.150 --> 00:22:39.090
Well, hold on a minute. What are you saying?

00:22:39.250 --> 00:22:40.590
You're saying you're playing

00:22:40.590 --> 00:22:42.230
as the Red October before that?

00:22:42.230 --> 00:22:43.210
You're not Sean Connery

00:22:43.210 --> 00:22:44.570
steering the Red October?

00:22:44.850 --> 00:22:48.410
Okay, are you playing as some guy in Gradius,

00:22:48.430 --> 00:22:50.010
or are you playing as the ship?

00:22:50.630 --> 00:22:52.770
You're not... Okay, that's a great question.

00:22:52.770 --> 00:22:57.130
You are controlling the Vic Viper in Gradius,

00:22:57.370 --> 00:22:58.730
but I hear you on that.

00:22:58.850 --> 00:23:01.650
I guess what I'm saying is that if Sean Connery...

00:23:01.650 --> 00:23:03.470
I was just drawing attention to the fact

00:23:03.470 --> 00:23:05.970
that now we're in some really weird, like,

00:23:07.390 --> 00:23:09.930
side-scrolling, like, platformer

00:23:09.930 --> 00:23:12.850
that makes no sense with what they've built

00:23:12.850 --> 00:23:14.050
with the rest of this game here.

00:23:14.050 --> 00:23:17.530
Did this kind of thing happen in the movie?

00:23:17.830 --> 00:23:19.970
Did Sean Connery, you know,

00:23:20.490 --> 00:23:22.030
start running around shooting people

00:23:22.030 --> 00:23:23.330
in a platforming setting?

00:23:23.830 --> 00:23:24.850
Actually, yes.

00:23:25.470 --> 00:23:27.710
Okay. Not at all.

00:23:29.210 --> 00:23:31.030
Again, you're looking at somebody

00:23:31.030 --> 00:23:32.470
that read the back flap,

00:23:32.850 --> 00:23:36.730
but, Mike, you said that you watched the movie,

00:23:36.750 --> 00:23:39.670
so I feel like you should know better.

00:23:39.670 --> 00:23:42.850
No, I don't think that there is...

00:23:42.850 --> 00:23:44.230
I mean, there's action in the movie,

00:23:44.290 --> 00:23:46.710
but nothing like what's happening in this level.

00:23:47.290 --> 00:23:49.250
Yeah, but there is, like, a...

00:23:49.250 --> 00:23:51.210
There is sabotaging.

00:23:51.730 --> 00:23:54.070
They don't have the circular bombs

00:23:54.070 --> 00:23:58.390
with a, like, a clock face, like, detonator,

00:23:59.230 --> 00:24:01.330
but there's, like, a saboteur

00:24:01.330 --> 00:24:05.390
and a face-off with guns and stuff,

00:24:05.390 --> 00:24:07.850
but I think this is just that them, like,

00:24:08.070 --> 00:24:09.710
oh, we have to make it...

00:24:09.710 --> 00:24:12.330
The movie was mostly in a submarine,

00:24:12.330 --> 00:24:14.850
so I guess we have to go into a submarine,

00:24:14.850 --> 00:24:18.470
even though we've built a complete, like,

00:24:19.150 --> 00:24:22.450
game and, like, way to play the game

00:24:22.450 --> 00:24:25.990
that this doesn't really, like, fit with at all.

00:24:27.450 --> 00:24:30.030
So it's a strange decision to do this.

00:24:30.230 --> 00:24:32.610
And yet, I don't really hate it.

00:24:32.610 --> 00:24:33.650
Like, it's a good...

00:24:33.650 --> 00:24:35.790
It's just good variety for the game.

00:24:35.930 --> 00:24:37.430
It's kind of weird that it didn't alternate

00:24:37.430 --> 00:24:38.310
between these

00:24:38.310 --> 00:24:40.470
and that it just introduces itself at the end here.

00:24:40.930 --> 00:24:43.590
I don't know. I think there's a huge quality drop

00:24:43.930 --> 00:24:45.110
when we get to this point.

00:24:45.210 --> 00:24:47.270
I feel like I'm playing... I'll be honest, I didn't get to that point,

00:24:47.310 --> 00:24:49.650
so I can't speak to the way it plays,

00:24:50.190 --> 00:24:52.290
but the way it looks, I think it is, like...

00:24:52.290 --> 00:24:54.590
I don't know. Part of me, like, I do want to appreciate,

00:24:55.350 --> 00:24:57.310
like, changing things up

00:24:57.310 --> 00:24:59.990
or having that, like, sort of...

00:25:00.950 --> 00:25:06.310
What's it called? Well, the spy manga game that we played.

00:25:06.870 --> 00:25:09.530
And we played it at the Long Island Retro Games Fest

00:25:09.530 --> 00:25:10.610
with a sniper rifle.

00:25:11.030 --> 00:25:11.950
Oh. It's also an NES.

00:25:12.030 --> 00:25:15.130
Golgo 13. Like, that Golgo 13-esque, like,

00:25:15.170 --> 00:25:16.450
oh, there's all these different ways of playing

00:25:16.450 --> 00:25:20.550
and everything. But, like, I feel like this game just, like, didn't...

00:25:20.890 --> 00:25:22.730
If it's just set up where 90% of the game

00:25:22.730 --> 00:25:23.610
is in the submarine, it's like,

00:25:23.650 --> 00:25:24.730
okay, now do this whole different thing

00:25:24.730 --> 00:25:25.850
that you're, like, not ready for.

00:25:26.290 --> 00:25:27.490
It's a little weird.

00:25:27.710 --> 00:25:28.830
I think that throws me off a little bit.

00:25:28.830 --> 00:25:30.370
Yeah, it's because you hated the opposite

00:25:30.370 --> 00:25:32.610
in Kid Icarus,

00:25:32.610 --> 00:25:34.710
where the whole game was a platformer

00:25:34.710 --> 00:25:36.850
and then turned into a shmup on the final level.

00:25:37.250 --> 00:25:38.950
Well, anything that turns into a shmup

00:25:39.510 --> 00:25:40.710
is not going to get my vote.

00:25:40.710 --> 00:25:42.090
No, but it was basically...

00:25:42.090 --> 00:25:44.890
The Hunt for Red October is a reverse Kid Icarus.

00:25:45.370 --> 00:25:48.550
Yeah. And, like, I'm not against that, though.

00:25:48.590 --> 00:25:50.170
Like, we've had other games that do that,

00:25:50.190 --> 00:25:51.230
and I'm like, oh, that's pretty cool.

00:25:51.230 --> 00:25:52.290
It's just, like...

00:25:52.290 --> 00:25:54.570
I guess having not gotten to it,

00:25:54.630 --> 00:25:55.930
I can only imagine that, like,

00:25:56.090 --> 00:25:57.390
it's so far into the game

00:25:57.390 --> 00:25:58.910
that I'm just, like, a little thrown off by it.

00:25:58.990 --> 00:26:00.430
It just feels like having to learn a new game.

00:26:00.610 --> 00:26:01.830
But, like, I don't know.

00:26:01.950 --> 00:26:03.130
I'm not fully opposed.

00:26:03.290 --> 00:26:04.590
I just... I guess I gotta get there.

00:26:04.590 --> 00:26:34.570
I guess I'll be right back.

00:26:50.730 --> 00:26:53.270
We were talking so much here about the end of the game

00:26:53.270 --> 00:26:54.450
that I feel like, you know,

00:26:54.530 --> 00:26:55.810
we only quickly glossed over

00:26:55.810 --> 00:26:56.890
that the beginning of the game

00:26:56.890 --> 00:26:58.730
starts with a heavy wall of text,

00:26:58.750 --> 00:27:01.130
but it's got a nice red background.

00:27:01.610 --> 00:27:02.650
And that's the kind of shit

00:27:02.650 --> 00:27:04.410
that I signed up for with Red October.

00:27:04.590 --> 00:27:06.930
There better be Red in the game.

00:27:07.010 --> 00:27:09.310
I think that they probably set aside, like,

00:27:09.410 --> 00:27:11.470
half of the memory in this game

00:27:11.470 --> 00:27:13.250
for just, like, the...

00:27:14.590 --> 00:27:16.130
for, like, the title sequence,

00:27:16.270 --> 00:27:19.090
which is very impressive,

00:27:19.090 --> 00:27:21.190
and I think, like, actually from the movie.

00:27:22.030 --> 00:27:23.310
Like, they have separate sprites.

00:27:23.310 --> 00:27:25.910
Yeah, yeah, the sonar turning into the hammer and sickle.

00:27:26.050 --> 00:27:27.010
Like, yeah, that came out really well.

00:27:27.010 --> 00:27:28.610
And then they move that into the corner

00:27:28.610 --> 00:27:29.750
and make it smaller,

00:27:29.770 --> 00:27:30.690
and it's like, oh, that's, like,

00:27:30.730 --> 00:27:31.950
three or four sprites right there

00:27:31.950 --> 00:27:33.370
that they keep cycling through.

00:27:33.870 --> 00:27:35.090
And then you go down,

00:27:35.150 --> 00:27:37.530
and then the whole title goes into the water

00:27:37.530 --> 00:27:40.350
and starts moving. Like, they didn't have that kind of technology.

00:27:40.610 --> 00:27:42.470
This is all, like, hand-keyed here.

00:27:42.590 --> 00:27:43.570
This is crazy.

00:27:43.570 --> 00:27:45.270
And then I thought they wouldn't have room

00:27:45.270 --> 00:27:46.410
for the game after that.

00:27:46.930 --> 00:27:48.730
Right, right. Or I thought the game was going to be

00:27:48.730 --> 00:27:49.730
way more impressive.

00:27:51.630 --> 00:27:54.590
Yeah, you have to insert cartridge two after that.

00:27:55.050 --> 00:27:58.930
Yeah. And, Joe, you mentioned that Paramount Pictures logo,

00:28:01.090 --> 00:28:02.290
but it's amazing.

00:28:02.490 --> 00:28:04.010
Like, they did a beautiful job on that.

00:28:04.270 --> 00:28:05.110
So it's not...

00:28:05.110 --> 00:28:07.070
I'm not just fanboying here

00:28:07.070 --> 00:28:08.670
that it's included in the game.

00:28:08.710 --> 00:28:09.890
I think they did it really nicely.

00:28:10.090 --> 00:28:11.550
And now I kind of want to see, like,

00:28:11.570 --> 00:28:14.210
all of the studio's logos on the NES.

00:28:14.810 --> 00:28:16.450
Yeah. Show me what the Warner Brothers logo...

00:28:16.450 --> 00:28:17.910
I can't say anything negative about the Paramount logo.

00:28:18.410 --> 00:28:19.650
But I don't work there anymore.

00:28:19.650 --> 00:28:20.610
I can say whatever I want.

00:28:20.650 --> 00:28:22.010
I never really liked that mountain.

00:28:22.550 --> 00:28:24.770
The Paramount logo is peak.

00:28:25.430 --> 00:28:27.230
Aha. Thank you.

00:28:27.910 --> 00:28:30.570
I'll be here all week. It's a pretty shit mountain, actually.

00:28:31.270 --> 00:28:33.170
Oh, interesting. Why?

00:28:33.530 --> 00:28:34.430
Just look at it.

00:28:35.030 --> 00:28:36.370
Oh, yeah. I do see it now.

00:28:36.710 --> 00:28:37.930
When you look at it.

00:28:37.950 --> 00:28:40.510
When you actually take one second and look at it.

00:28:40.730 --> 00:28:43.010
Right. They did get the proportions a little off.

00:28:43.170 --> 00:28:45.390
Like, Paramount is very clearly red and everything,

00:28:45.510 --> 00:28:47.150
but, like, the mountain isn't proportionally red.

00:28:47.150 --> 00:28:48.650
Yeah, it's, like, half of it's missing.

00:28:48.830 --> 00:28:50.910
No, I mean, even, like, in the movies.

00:28:50.950 --> 00:28:52.210
The real mountain, yeah.

00:28:52.410 --> 00:28:55.310
It's kind of shit. Was it...

00:28:55.310 --> 00:28:56.990
This is just me being stupid for a second.

00:28:57.210 --> 00:28:59.370
Like, the original Paramount Pictures logo,

00:28:59.610 --> 00:29:01.430
like, did they actually film a real mountain,

00:29:01.470 --> 00:29:03.310
or is that, like, a drawer?

00:29:03.470 --> 00:29:04.650
Is that, like, an art painting?

00:29:04.650 --> 00:29:06.830
They didn't teach you that in Paramount school?

00:29:06.990 --> 00:29:08.570
They didn't teach me that in Paramount school,

00:29:08.650 --> 00:29:10.810
but I know that that was a real lion for MGM.

00:29:11.690 --> 00:29:13.590
Really? Yes.

00:29:13.750 --> 00:29:14.750
That was... Wait, are you being serious?

00:29:14.750 --> 00:29:16.050
I thought it was a painting.

00:29:18.090 --> 00:29:19.190
The Damian Roar. It was a flip book.

00:29:19.670 --> 00:29:21.550
Yeah. Well, okay. Well, I got news for both of you.

00:29:21.710 --> 00:29:23.250
The Columbia Lady is a painting,

00:29:23.250 --> 00:29:25.910
so this isn't a crazy question to ask about the mountain.

00:29:26.630 --> 00:29:27.530
I don't think it's crazy.

00:29:27.670 --> 00:29:30.690
I just assume it's a painting, but...

00:29:30.690 --> 00:29:32.410
Yeah, it probably is.

00:29:32.690 --> 00:29:34.530
But I wonder if it's based on a real mountain.

00:29:35.790 --> 00:29:38.290
It's based... Yeah, it's based on Paramount Mountain.

00:29:39.310 --> 00:29:40.610
This is good shit, guys.

00:29:40.930 --> 00:29:42.090
This is really good stuff.

00:29:42.090 --> 00:29:44.890
All right, so let's see.

00:29:45.370 --> 00:29:46.410
Cinematic intent?

00:29:47.170 --> 00:29:48.210
Cinematic intent.

00:29:48.590 --> 00:29:50.670
The game is going for it.

00:29:50.810 --> 00:29:54.990
Does it land it? I described it when we first started.

00:29:55.130 --> 00:29:57.850
This is a very polished game,

00:29:58.170 --> 00:30:05.090
and I think while it's not cinematic insofar as it feels like a movie,

00:30:05.090 --> 00:30:11.150
or even is trying to follow what happens in this movie very much,

00:30:12.030 --> 00:30:17.110
I think at least the first 70% of this game,

00:30:17.250 --> 00:30:22.530
when you're controlling the submarine,

00:30:22.810 --> 00:30:26.610
I think it can lean sort of cinematic.

00:30:26.610 --> 00:30:28.770
Like, the explosions are cool.

00:30:30.250 --> 00:30:31.890
There's high tension.

00:30:32.650 --> 00:30:34.750
And then it kind of throws it all out the window

00:30:34.750 --> 00:30:37.230
when you play regular Mario Brothers at the end.

00:30:37.410 --> 00:30:39.950
But yeah, I think some of it is cinematic.

00:30:40.430 --> 00:30:43.930
I don't know if this is what would translate it to cinematic,

00:30:43.930 --> 00:30:45.470
but it is like...

00:30:45.470 --> 00:30:48.190
Visually, it does look very nice.

00:30:48.350 --> 00:30:52.130
Like, the color palettes all feel really good,

00:30:52.170 --> 00:30:53.890
but also the texture of everything.

00:30:53.890 --> 00:30:57.450
I mean, I think it's in the second level where everything looks like crystal-y,

00:30:57.490 --> 00:30:58.330
we were talking about.

00:30:58.910 --> 00:31:02.330
And then later levels, there's really interesting shadows

00:31:02.330 --> 00:31:05.030
and the stalactites and stalagmites.

00:31:05.530 --> 00:31:10.870
It looks like one of those games that looks a little closer to...

00:31:11.970 --> 00:31:13.910
I don't want to say it's like a next-gen,

00:31:14.010 --> 00:31:15.290
like it's not Super Nintendo levels,

00:31:15.450 --> 00:31:16.550
but it's like that in-between,

00:31:16.790 --> 00:31:22.070
where there's a lot of good shading and just art in it that looks nice.

00:31:22.070 --> 00:31:24.570
Yeah, this looks pretty close to Sniss.

00:31:25.030 --> 00:31:27.090
Right, we wouldn't have saw this in 1986.

00:31:27.570 --> 00:31:31.110
Right. And so far, the game has been compared to Gradius,

00:31:31.190 --> 00:31:33.550
but in a submarine, and Mario, but with a gun.

00:31:33.810 --> 00:31:37.070
And so, by all means, this game sounds amazing.

00:31:37.330 --> 00:31:40.290
Yeah, like, anything else you guys want to say about...

00:31:40.290 --> 00:31:41.610
compare this game to some other games?

00:31:41.690 --> 00:31:43.470
Because we're doing a great job.

00:31:43.470 --> 00:31:47.590
I will say that you are mischaracterizing how I said Gradius.

00:31:47.590 --> 00:31:50.150
You were talking about being Sean Connery.

00:31:50.730 --> 00:31:51.910
And that's why I...

00:31:51.910 --> 00:31:53.110
Okay, so I got a question for you.

00:31:53.350 --> 00:31:57.850
In 007 Agent Under Fire on the PlayStation 2,

00:31:58.230 --> 00:32:00.910
when you get into the Aston Martin,

00:32:00.990 --> 00:32:04.530
but you've been playing as James Bond,

00:32:04.870 --> 00:32:06.630
are you now the Aston Martin,

00:32:06.690 --> 00:32:08.930
or are you still just James Bond driving the Aston Martin?

00:32:08.930 --> 00:32:09.870
That is an example.

00:32:10.230 --> 00:32:11.810
I want you to point, Mr.

00:32:11.970 --> 00:32:13.150
Person that's seen the movie,

00:32:13.810 --> 00:32:16.390
to any moment in which Sean Connery

00:32:16.390 --> 00:32:18.690
touches a piece of equipment on the submarine.

00:32:19.310 --> 00:32:20.930
He's not driving the submarine.

00:32:21.410 --> 00:32:22.770
It's true, it's true.

00:32:22.950 --> 00:32:24.670
Actually, yeah, there's an entire fleet in there.

00:32:24.830 --> 00:32:25.770
So, yeah, that's a good...

00:32:25.770 --> 00:32:26.690
It's a great point.

00:32:26.910 --> 00:32:30.450
We can't figure out who is currently piloting this.

00:32:30.510 --> 00:32:34.990
Is he commanding the people piloting the submarine?

00:32:35.490 --> 00:32:39.050
Yes. In which case, I think you're playing as the neurons in his brain

00:32:39.050 --> 00:32:40.170
that are going through his mouth,

00:32:40.170 --> 00:32:41.750
telling him to speak to those people.

00:32:43.430 --> 00:32:45.290
Perfect. Perfect conversation.

00:32:45.370 --> 00:32:47.530
Feels like one we've had many times before.

00:32:48.270 --> 00:32:50.570
Just like how at the end of every episode,

00:32:50.570 --> 00:32:51.850
we have the same conversation,

00:32:51.850 --> 00:32:53.890
which is the essential games list.

00:32:57.550 --> 00:33:02.430
Joe? Well, I think this game does a few things right,

00:33:02.430 --> 00:33:05.410
like the way it feels to control the submarine,

00:33:05.410 --> 00:33:07.490
the look of the game.

00:33:08.610 --> 00:33:09.570
I think overall,

00:33:10.110 --> 00:33:12.330
I don't know if it's just that this game is too hard,

00:33:12.850 --> 00:33:16.470
but navigating in this game is very frustrating to me.

00:33:16.650 --> 00:33:17.590
And not because...

00:33:17.590 --> 00:33:20.810
I don't think it's because it controls poorly.

00:33:20.810 --> 00:33:21.970
I think it's just because

00:33:23.130 --> 00:33:26.530
sometimes you have to really thread the needle.

00:33:26.770 --> 00:33:29.510
And I get that that's where the challenge comes from in this,

00:33:29.510 --> 00:33:34.010
but for me, this was just death after death after death

00:33:34.010 --> 00:33:35.530
to the point where it's like...

00:33:36.210 --> 00:33:38.210
It's touchy. And I know it's touchy on purpose.

00:33:38.210 --> 00:33:39.970
I know that's what it's trying to do.

00:33:40.050 --> 00:33:43.730
But I think that they accidentally made it feel

00:33:43.730 --> 00:33:44.910
a little unbalanced.

00:33:45.070 --> 00:33:47.590
And as much as there's some cool things in this game,

00:33:48.230 --> 00:33:49.370
it's not very fun,

00:33:49.390 --> 00:33:50.610
I guess is what I should say.

00:33:50.670 --> 00:33:52.510
I didn't have a good time playing it.

00:33:52.510 --> 00:33:55.730
I have a good time watching videos about it

00:33:55.730 --> 00:33:56.950
and thinking about it afterwards,

00:33:57.130 --> 00:33:58.370
but I'm not like...

00:33:58.370 --> 00:34:01.370
Oh, yeah. In the moment, it's not fun.

00:34:01.450 --> 00:34:02.930
It's a frustrating experience for me.

00:34:03.230 --> 00:34:05.950
So I'm going to say not essential.

00:34:06.490 --> 00:34:10.110
Sean? Yeah, I enjoyed most of this game.

00:34:11.610 --> 00:34:15.430
I did like the shmup parts.

00:34:15.430 --> 00:34:17.450
I think this is actually one of the better shmups

00:34:17.450 --> 00:34:20.010
that we've ever played. And I'm going to continue to call it a shmup.

00:34:22.490 --> 00:34:25.050
But I'm not going to say that it's essential.

00:34:25.350 --> 00:34:29.130
The whole third act kind of ruins it for me.

00:34:30.110 --> 00:34:33.550
And even if it was just the submarine parts,

00:34:33.550 --> 00:34:35.730
I don't think it was essential worthy.

00:34:37.270 --> 00:34:39.430
But it looks cool.

00:34:39.630 --> 00:34:40.690
It plays nice.

00:34:41.810 --> 00:34:43.430
I'd recommend playing it

00:34:43.430 --> 00:34:44.910
if you're into that sort of thing.

00:34:44.910 --> 00:34:48.370
Or if you just want to...

00:34:48.370 --> 00:34:50.330
If you want to hunt the Red October

00:34:50.330 --> 00:34:52.730
or be hunted as the Red October

00:34:52.730 --> 00:34:55.110
that sort of does it for you,

00:34:55.170 --> 00:34:56.550
then I'd play it.

00:34:56.830 --> 00:34:57.910
But not essential.

00:34:58.230 --> 00:34:59.550
The Hunt for Red October

00:34:59.550 --> 00:35:02.430
is a less than faithful recreation

00:35:02.430 --> 00:35:03.950
of the story of the movie

00:35:03.950 --> 00:35:05.190
and probably the book.

00:35:05.250 --> 00:35:06.210
I don't even know how much

00:35:06.210 --> 00:35:07.950
the movie differentiates from the book.

00:35:07.950 --> 00:35:11.530
But one thing that maybe we should have talked about

00:35:11.530 --> 00:35:13.090
instead of rambling through the episode

00:35:13.090 --> 00:35:14.310
is that it does,

00:35:14.490 --> 00:35:17.250
in a video game-y way,

00:35:17.530 --> 00:35:20.630
it preserves that escape and pursuit premise

00:35:20.630 --> 00:35:22.270
from the game pretty well.

00:35:24.450 --> 00:35:26.190
Yes, they've added in

00:35:26.190 --> 00:35:28.150
a comical amount,

00:35:28.270 --> 00:35:29.690
like an armada against you.

00:35:29.790 --> 00:35:31.730
And that's not what the movie is like at all.

00:35:31.830 --> 00:35:32.890
But there still is this,

00:35:34.390 --> 00:35:35.450
not thriller,

00:35:35.450 --> 00:35:37.630
but tense throughout the game

00:35:37.630 --> 00:35:38.830
of being the sub

00:35:38.830 --> 00:35:41.210
and having to dodge a barrage

00:35:41.210 --> 00:35:43.210
of both environmental

00:35:43.210 --> 00:35:45.950
and military conflict.

00:35:46.330 --> 00:35:48.210
And so I think it does that really well.

00:35:48.390 --> 00:35:51.370
It is fun to be the Red October,

00:35:51.990 --> 00:35:53.710
but not something I would have had

00:35:53.710 --> 00:35:55.610
on my wish list at any point.

00:35:55.770 --> 00:35:56.930
Like, I guess that makes me think about,

00:35:57.050 --> 00:35:59.350
like, what other movies

00:35:59.350 --> 00:36:00.910
that shouldn't really be video games

00:36:00.910 --> 00:36:01.930
would I actually be, like,

00:36:02.010 --> 00:36:03.650
interested in playing after the fact?

00:36:03.650 --> 00:36:04.610
I don't know.

00:36:04.870 --> 00:36:06.170
But this one definitely,

00:36:07.970 --> 00:36:09.450
while it doesn't stand out

00:36:09.450 --> 00:36:10.610
for any particular reason,

00:36:10.850 --> 00:36:13.410
they actually did do a good job

00:36:13.410 --> 00:36:15.350
of not just, like, using the title

00:36:15.350 --> 00:36:16.310
to hunt for Red October

00:36:16.310 --> 00:36:18.390
and making a completely different game.

00:36:18.390 --> 00:36:20.930
I don't think the Switch at the end

00:36:23.490 --> 00:36:25.650
is either weird or unfair.

00:36:25.650 --> 00:36:27.490
I think it's just something else

00:36:27.490 --> 00:36:28.750
to throw into a game

00:36:28.750 --> 00:36:30.530
that's trying a lot of things.

00:36:31.210 --> 00:36:32.310
It's difficulty

00:36:32.310 --> 00:36:36.530
and barrage of enemies

00:36:36.530 --> 00:36:38.630
is, like, maybe a little too much for me.

00:36:39.370 --> 00:36:40.770
But I do like that

00:36:40.770 --> 00:36:42.490
it actually does build

00:36:42.490 --> 00:36:43.850
the Red October itself

00:36:43.850 --> 00:36:45.690
into, as I mentioned,

00:36:45.770 --> 00:36:46.690
with all those different controls,

00:36:47.090 --> 00:36:48.150
into something that is

00:36:48.150 --> 00:36:49.970
cool to control

00:36:49.970 --> 00:36:53.570
and interesting to navigate around with.

00:36:53.570 --> 00:36:56.790
You can't just spam torpedoes

00:36:56.790 --> 00:36:57.750
and make it, like,

00:36:57.790 --> 00:36:58.950
another one of those shmups

00:36:58.950 --> 00:36:59.950
where you're just holding down

00:36:59.950 --> 00:37:02.550
the turbo button. You also have to be aware

00:37:02.550 --> 00:37:04.630
of things coming at you from above

00:37:04.630 --> 00:37:06.270
and when to use your

00:37:06.270 --> 00:37:07.650
caterpillar drive

00:37:07.650 --> 00:37:10.010
and when to use your decoys.

00:37:10.210 --> 00:37:12.390
So I do think that the game overall

00:37:13.830 --> 00:37:15.530
does a great job of

00:37:15.530 --> 00:37:17.590
making a movie video game.

00:37:17.590 --> 00:37:18.970
I just don't think it's actually

00:37:18.970 --> 00:37:20.370
that great of a video game.

00:37:20.530 --> 00:37:22.250
So no for me either.

00:37:22.250 --> 00:37:23.350
That's three no's.

00:37:24.690 --> 00:37:26.150
But not the, like,

00:37:26.490 --> 00:37:28.490
not the worst movie entry we've had

00:37:28.490 --> 00:37:29.370
and allegedly

00:37:30.210 --> 00:37:31.610
a lot of people from the movie

00:37:31.610 --> 00:37:33.470
are in this unlike Back to the Future

00:37:33.470 --> 00:37:34.790
where we couldn't even get Doc.

00:37:35.370 --> 00:37:37.310
Yeah, even Sean Connery was in it.

00:37:38.070 --> 00:37:39.370
And as the...

00:37:39.370 --> 00:37:40.950
But now, looking back at it,

00:37:41.030 --> 00:37:42.070
now I'm realizing that

00:37:42.070 --> 00:37:43.610
Sean Connery would have been

00:37:43.610 --> 00:37:44.990
a lot younger than I'm imagining

00:37:44.990 --> 00:37:46.010
he would be in this movie

00:37:46.010 --> 00:37:47.550
because it was, you know,

00:37:47.770 --> 00:37:50.070
what, 1990. But, uh...

